    "<div style=\"border:2px solid #6C8196; border-radius:12px; padding:18px 20px; margin-bottom:18px; background-color:rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\">\n",
    "\n",
    "  <div style=\"color:#6C8196; font-size:24px; font-weight:700; display:inline-block; border-bottom:3px solid #6C8196; padding-bottom:4px; margin-bottom:10px;\">\n",
    "    Plan Execution Summary\n",
    "  </div>\n",
    "\n",
    "  <div style=\"color:#0D0A53; font-size:15px; line-height:1.7; margin-top:10px;\">\n",
    "    The main steps from the original plan were completed successfully. The project began with loading and inspecting the four source datasets, followed by checking data quality, validating the target logic, and understanding how the tables should be combined through <code>customerID</code>. After that, the data was merged into one customer-level dataset, key preprocessing tasks were performed, and new features were engineered to support the churn prediction task.\n",
    "    <br><br>\n",
    "    The modeling stage was also completed as planned. Several classification models were trained and compared, after which the strongest model was selected and evaluated on the test set. No major parts of the original workflow were skipped. However, one methodological improvement was introduced during implementation: instead of selecting the final model directly from test-set performance, the models were compared using cross-validation on the training set only. This made the evaluation process more rigorous and ensured that the final test results reflected true out-of-sample performance.\n",
    "  </div>\n",
    "\n",
    "  <div style=\"color:#2C5839; font-size:15px; line-height:1.7; margin-top:18px; padding-top:12px; border-top:1.5px solid #6C8196;\">\n",
    "    Outcome: the planned workflow was fully carried out, with a small methodological refinement that improved the reliability of model selection.\n",
    "  </div>\n",
    "\n",
    "</div>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<div style=\"border:2px solid #6C8196; border-radius:12px; padding:18px 20px; margin-bottom:18px; background-color:rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\">\n",
    "\n",
    "  <div style=\"color:#6C8196; font-size:24px; font-weight:700; display:inline-block; border-bottom:3px solid #6C8196; padding-bottom:4px; margin-bottom:10px;\">\n",
    "    Difficulties Encountered and How They Were Solved\n",
    "  </div>\n",
    "\n",
    "  <div style=\"color:#0D0A53; font-size:15px; line-height:1.7; margin-top:10px;\">\n",
    "    Several difficulties appeared during the implementation of the project, but each of them was manageable after careful inspection of the data. One of the main challenges was interpreting the target correctly. The <code>EndDate</code> column mixed the value <code>\"No\"</code> with actual contract termination dates, so it was necessary to confirm how churn should be defined from a business perspective before building the model.\n",
    "    <br><br>\n",
    "    Another difficulty was related to data preprocessing. The <code>TotalCharges</code> column was stored as text and contained hidden blank values that were not visible in a standard missing-value check. After inspecting those rows more closely, it became clear that they belonged to newly joined customers who had not yet accumulated total charges, so the column was converted to numeric and those blank values were handled accordingly. A further challenge came from the <code>internet</code> and <code>phone</code> tables, which did not contain all customers. This was resolved by interpreting absent matches as meaningful lack of service rather than as random missing data.\n",
    "    <br><br>\n",
    "    A final methodological difficulty involved model evaluation. An initial comparison based directly on the test set was less rigorous than desired, so the workflow was improved by selecting the best model through cross-validation on the training set only, followed by one final evaluation on the untouched test set.\n",
    "  </div>\n",
    "\n",
    "  <div style=\"color:#2C5839; font-size:15px; line-height:1.7; margin-top:18px; padding-top:12px; border-top:1.5px solid #6C8196;\">\n",
    "    Result: the main challenges were resolved through careful data interpretation, targeted preprocessing, and a cleaner evaluation strategy.\n",
    "  </div>\n",
    "\n",
    "</div>"
   ]
  },
  {
   "cell_type": "markdown",
   "metadata": {},
   "source": [
    "<div style=\"border:2px solid #6C8196; border-radius:12px; padding:18px 20px; margin-bottom:18px; background-color:rgba(255,255,255,0.08);\">\n",
    "\n",
    "  <div style=\"color:#6C8196; font-size:24px; font-weight:700; display:inline-block; border-bottom:3px solid #6C8196; padding-bottom:4px; margin-bottom:10px;\">\n",
    "    Key Steps in Solving the Task\n",
    "  </div>\n",
    "\n",
    "  <div style=\"color:#0D0A53; font-size:15px; line-height:1.8; margin-top:10px;\">\n",
    "    - The first key step was integrating the four source tables into one customer-level dataset using <code>customerID</code>. This created a unified analytical view combining contract details, personal data, internet services, and phone services.\n",
    "    <br><br>\n",
    "    - The second key step was preprocessing the data carefully. This included defining the target from <code>EndDate</code>, converting date fields into usable formats, transforming <code>TotalCharges</code> from text to numeric form, and resolving hidden blank values.\n",
    "    <br><br>\n",
    "    - Another important step was handling service-related missing matches correctly. Customers absent from the <code>internet</code> or <code>phone</code> tables were interpreted as customers without those services, rather than as random missing data.\n",
    "    <br><br>\n",
    "    - Feature engineering also played an important role in the final solution. Variables such as estimated tenure, contract start components, and total subscribed services were created to provide the models with more informative predictors.\n",
    "    <br><br>\n",
    "    - The final key step was building a consistent modeling workflow. Numeric and categorical variables were processed through a shared pipeline, multiple models were compared using cross-validation on the training set, and the strongest model was then evaluated once on the untouched test set.\n",
    "  </div>\n",
    "\n",
    "  <div style=\"color:#2C5839; font-size:15px; line-height:1.7; margin-top:18px; padding-top:12px; border-top:1.5px solid #6C8196;\">\n",
    "    Result: the project was solved through strong data integration, careful preprocessing, meaningful feature engineering, and reliable model evaluation.\n",
    "  </div>\n",
    "\n",
    "</div>"
   ]
  },
